[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429529\">7015A04</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429538\">7015B30</a></p><p>1. Release the control (1a or 1b) from its housing and keep it.</p><p>2. If necessary, release the rubber diaphragm (2a or 2b) from the\nhousing.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045178.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check the control is undamaged.</p><p>Fit the rubber diaphragm in position.</p><p>Attach the control device in position.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429538\">7015B30</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429529\">7015A04</a></p>"]]